{"kind":"node","id":"invariant:resolver-precedence","type":"Invariant","name":"Node resolution has deterministic precedence","description":"Resolution tries exact node ID, then case-insensitive alias, then a unique partial ID or name match."}
{"kind":"node","id":"invariant:bounded-graph-retrieval","type":"Invariant","name":"Traversal and paths are bounded","description":"Traversal expands a frontier only to the requested depth and optional predicate set; shortest path stops at max depth."}
{"kind":"node","id":"invariant:gold-recall-coverage","type":"Invariant","name":"Gold evaluation measures expected-node recall","description":"A check passes when every expected node is retrieved from its seeds; extra nodes do not fail the check."}
{"kind":"node","id":"invariant:build-surfaces-evidence-status","type":"Invariant","name":"Build surfaces evidence freshness","description":"A build requires valid resolvable evidence, then records fresh, stale, or unlocked lock status in the generated SQLite index rather than treating freshness as a build gate."}
{"kind":"node","id":"invariant:review-state-is-procedural","type":"Invariant","name":"Review state is procedural metadata","description":"The CLI validates review labels and retains them in the index, but candidate isolation and promotion remain orchestrator responsibilities rather than an identity-attested authorization boundary."}
